a</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Li</surname><given-names>H-C</given-names></name><name><surname>Suzuki</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Microvascular mechanisms of change in tumor blood flow due to angiotensin II, epinephrine, and methoxamine: a functional morphometric study</article-title><source>Cancer Res</source><year>1993</year><volume>53</volume><fpage>5528</fpage><lpage>5534</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Cancer Res||53|5528||bib6|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8221694</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Li</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Hori</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Saito</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Tanda</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Suzuki</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The effects of angiotensin II and other noradrenergic vasoconstrictors on the blood flow in Yoshida rat ascites hepatoma AH109A at same electrode position</article-title><source>Gan To Kagaku Ryoho</source><year>1990</year><volume>17</volume><fpage>548</fpage><lpage>553</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Gan To Kagaku Ryoho||17|548||bib12|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1969726</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nihei</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Suga</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Morinaga</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Ohishi</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Okano</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Ohsumi</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Hatanaka</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Naka